  A CHECK OF MINE THAT ASSERTED A DEFECT, AND THE PRODUCT WAS RIGHT. The first version claimed an
  un-parked row is DISPATCHED in the same tick. It is not, deliberately: an answered row returns to
  `dispatched` because the executor already holds it, and re-spawning would run the same
  item twice. Asserting the convenient thing would have pinned a defect (tests-can-pin-defects); the
  ordering claim belongs on the SOURCE, where it now is.
  SOURCE-ORDER ASSERTION ADDED TO test_serverdown.py, as BOSS asked and in the file whose green was
  over-read, so the next reader meets the correction beside the claim.
  CRASH IS NEITHER CATCH NOR MISS. The source-order checks used `str.index`, which RAISES when the
  term is deleted — the first mutation run ended in `ValueError: substring not found` after 11 clean
  reds. Replaced with a helper where a missing term is a clean False.
